      <div class="pf-info-bar" style="margin-top:2rem;">
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text);font-weight:600;">1 hour minimum on all Formby call-outs. After the first hour we charge in 30 minute blocks. Parts at cost. Written quote before any work begins.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>


  <!-- FORMBY PROPERTY KNOWLEDGE - UNIQUE SECTION -->
  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="pf-section-label">LOCAL EXPERTISE</span>
      <h2>Formby Properties. What Our Engineers Find.</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Formby is one of Merseyside's most affluent residential areas. The properties here are larger, the systems are more complex, and when something goes wrong at 11pm, you need an engineer who knows what they are looking at.</p>

      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1.5rem;margin-top:2rem;">

        <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
            <div style="background:var(--orange);color:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:0.3rem 0.7rem;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:900;font-size:0.85rem;white-space:nowrap;flex-shrink:0;">L37</div>
            <div>
              <strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Executive Homes with Multi-Bathroom Systems</strong>
              <p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">Formby's larger detached and semi-detached homes often have three or more bathrooms, pressurised heating systems and unvented hot water cylinders. When a fault hits a multi-bathroom home, the damage is much worse than in a simple single-bathroom terrace. A leaking cylinder or failed pump can hit water and heating across a big house very fast. Our engineers hold G3 training for unvented cylinder work and are fully kitted out to diagnose and repair multi-zone heating. We work on Formby's private estates often and carry the right stock for high-spec plumbing.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
            <div style="background:var(--orange);color:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:0.3rem 0.7rem;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:900;font-size:0.85rem;white-space:nowrap;flex-shrink:0;">FRESHFIELD</div>
            <div>
              <strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">The Pine Roads and Period Properties</strong>
              <p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">Freshfield has some of Formby's most distinct period homes, including the well-known Pine Roads area with its National Trust surroundings. Homes here range from big 1900s and inter-war houses to 1960s and 1970s bungalows. Freshfield bungalows are especially prone to frozen pipes in cold weather because pipework runs in loft spaces right below exposed roof sections, with little insulation in some cases. We work on Freshfield homes often for both emergency call-outs and planned work, and we know the mix of homes in this part of L37.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
            <div style="background:var(--orange);color:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:0.3rem 0.7rem;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:900;font-size:0.85rem;white-space:nowrap;flex-shrink:0;">COASTAL</div>
            <div>
              <strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Sandy Ground and Coastal Conditions</strong>
              <p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">Formby sits on the Lancashire coastal plain and the sandy soil means ground movement is more common than in clay-heavy inland areas. Over time this can stress underground pipe joints, leading to slow leaks that turn into emergencies. Being close to the Irish Sea also brings salt air that speeds up rust on any outdoor pipework, taps and fittings. Homes closest to the dune system and beach at Formby Point see this most. We know how to find and fix pipe failures from ground movement and salt corrosion from Formby's coastal air.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="pf-card pf-card-left-orange">
          <div style="display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:flex-start;">
            <div style="background:var(--orange);color:#fff;border-radius:6px;padding:0.3rem 0.7rem;font-family:'Barlow Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:900;font-size:0.85rem;white-space:nowrap;flex-shrink:0;">HIGHTOWN</div>
            <div>
              <strong style="display:block;color:var(--navy);font-size:1rem;margin-bottom:0.35rem;">Hightown and Ince Blundell</strong>
              <p style="font-size:0.93rem;color:var(--muted);margin:0;line-height:1.65;">The villages south of Formby, including Hightown and Ince Blundell, have a mix of older village properties and newer private developments. Hightown in particular has older homes along the coastal road where outdoor pipework has been hit by decades of sea air. These villages are quieter and less built-up than Formby itself. When a plumbing emergency hits late at night, you need to know your plumber will actually turn up. We attend Hightown and Ince Blundell at any hour, 365 days a year, at the same rates as everywhere else.</p>
